**Constructor overloading:** several constructors with different parameter lists.

```java
class Student {
    String name; int age;
    Student() { this("Unknown", 0); }
    Student(String name) { this(name, 0); }
    Student(String name, int age) { this.name = name; this.age = age; }
}
```

**Main overloading.** You can write `main(int x)` or `main(String s)` in the same class, but the JVM starts only from `public static void main(String[] args)`. The others are normal methods and run only if you call them, for example `main(5)` from the real `main`.

**Static method from main.** `static int square(int n) { return n * n; }` can be called directly as `square(4)` from `main` since both are static. An instance method needs an object first: `new Demo().show()`.

**Even or odd:** `n % 2 == 0`. **Reverse a string:** `new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString()`, or a loop from the last character to the first.

**Valid parentheses** (stack, O(n)):

```java
static boolean valid(String s) {
    Deque<Character> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
    for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '{' || c == '[') st.push(c);
        else {
            if (st.isEmpty()) return false;
            char o = st.pop();
            if ((c == ')' && o != '(') || (c == '}' && o != '{') || (c == ']' && o != '[')) return false;
        }
    }
    return st.isEmpty();
}
```

**Renaming the main class.** If the class is `public`, the file name must match: renaming `class Main` to `class App` while the file is `Main.java` gives *"class App is public, should be declared in a file named App.java"*. If you compile fine but run `java Main` after renaming, you get *"Could not find or load main class Main"* (`ClassNotFoundException`). Fix: make the file name, class name and the `java` command all agree. Also check IDE run configurations that still reference the old name.
